- Let me try and answer it.

00:25:05.160 --> 00:25:06.132
- Okay.
- No actually no,

00:25:06.132 --> 00:25:08.000
I want you to go first and I will follow,

00:25:08.000 --> 00:25:09.340
but you should try and answer it,

00:25:09.340 --> 00:25:10.440
don't deflect, you go.

00:25:11.870 --> 00:25:15.070
Do you smell that, it's like--
- It's like a bakery

00:25:15.070 --> 00:25:16.330
or something downstairs.

00:25:16.330 --> 00:25:18.212
- Someone just kicked on the,
- I know,

00:25:18.212 --> 00:25:19.320
smell like cinnamon buns.
- The pancakes

00:25:19.320 --> 00:25:21.600
or the cinnamon buns, oh my goodness.

00:25:21.600 --> 00:25:23.270
If you're at home listening and watching

00:25:23.270 --> 00:25:24.700
I'm so bummed you can't smell

00:25:24.700 --> 00:25:27.740
how good it smells in
this this beautiful spot

00:25:27.740 --> 00:25:29.590
that we're in here, in hoe Ace hotel.

00:25:30.860 --> 00:25:35.860
- There was a defining moment
for me in this whole journey

00:25:36.330 --> 00:25:40.110
and it was after I had done

00:25:42.330 --> 00:25:44.580
the five Ironman thing.

00:25:44.580 --> 00:25:49.200
And I was noticing that the
media was taking an interest

00:25:49.200 --> 00:25:51.480
in what I was doing which
as I mentioned earlier

00:25:51.480 --> 00:25:52.900
was kind of a bizarre thing.

00:25:52.900 --> 00:25:55.653
'Cause I was just doing this for myself.

00:25:56.670 --> 00:26:00.210
CNN, Sanjay Gupta came to my
house did like a piece on me

00:26:00.210 --> 00:26:03.980
and they asked, the people at CNN asked me

00:26:03.980 --> 00:26:07.540
to write a guest blog posts for cnn.com.

00:26:07.540 --> 00:26:11.310
Which I did and it's the
little like here's my story

00:26:12.250 --> 00:26:14.720
and that got published and
it was tracking so well

00:26:14.720 --> 00:26:17.130
that they put it on the CNN homepage.

00:26:17.130 --> 00:26:19.140
And it became like the most emailed story

00:26:19.140 --> 00:26:22.080
for you know 48 hours or 72
hours something like that.

00:26:22.080 --> 00:26:25.610
Like it just hit a nerve and
it like track really well.

00:26:25.610 --> 00:26:29.500
And I just got shellacked
with emails all of a sudden.

00:26:29.500 --> 00:26:31.280
I mean this was really like,

00:26:31.280 --> 00:26:35.750
I had never been like a
public person in any regard.

00:26:35.750 --> 00:26:39.690
And some of these emails that came in

00:26:39.690 --> 00:26:42.220
were just so touching and unbelievable,

00:26:42.220 --> 00:26:45.570
like I told my story in a vulnerable way

00:26:45.570 --> 00:26:49.610
and it gave people permission
to then tell me their story.

00:26:49.610 --> 00:26:52.080
And I got these long you
know multi paragraph emails

00:26:52.080 --> 00:26:53.550
like this is what happened to me

00:26:53.550 --> 00:26:54.780
and this is what I went through

00:26:54.780 --> 00:26:57.500
and here's my struggles and my pain.

00:26:57.500 --> 00:27:02.140
And I was just so touched at the feeling

00:27:02.140 --> 00:27:03.990
of trust that these people had.

00:27:03.990 --> 00:27:06.950
And I think it was very emotional for me

00:27:06.950 --> 00:27:08.230
to like read all these emails.

00:27:08.230 --> 00:27:13.100
And it made me realize that
the path forward for me

00:27:13.100 --> 00:27:17.970
and where I can really
serve is to be a cipher

00:27:17.970 --> 00:27:21.270
for these people on the
path to transformation.

00:27:21.270 --> 00:27:25.640
If I can be like a home
base or a safe place

00:27:25.640 --> 00:27:29.620
for them to come to, to
confide in or to look to

00:27:29.620 --> 00:27:32.860
for inspiration and guidance
for what the next step

00:27:32.860 --> 00:27:35.530
for them might be, that
perhaps I had something

00:27:35.530 --> 00:27:37.170
to say in that regard.

00:27:37.170 --> 00:27:39.520
And so building upon that has really been

00:27:41.375 --> 00:27:44.540
what I've done ever since that moment.

00:27:44.540 --> 00:27:47.820
- It's interesting that there
is a true north inside of you.

00:27:47.820 --> 00:27:51.426
You access that through
vulnerability, right?

00:27:51.426 --> 00:27:54.657
You wrote your story out
and people responded to it,

00:27:54.657 --> 00:27:56.090
and that gave you a feeling

00:27:56.090 --> 00:27:57.610
and it was the feeling that you looked at

00:27:57.610 --> 00:28:00.910
like wait a minute, this is a sign.

00:28:00.910 --> 00:28:01.743
- [Rich] Yeah.

00:28:01.743 --> 00:28:02.576
- That I'm doing the thing,

00:28:02.576 --> 00:28:04.093
you talked to earlier about intuition.

00:28:05.720 --> 00:28:08.990
Is that the same feeling,
this awareness that you had

00:28:08.990 --> 00:28:10.180
once you'd put your,

00:28:10.180 --> 00:28:11.840
you had to take the first step obviously.

00:28:11.840 --> 00:28:13.160
- Right.
- Because CNN says

00:28:13.160 --> 00:28:15.200
you wanna write this you say no,

00:28:15.200 --> 00:28:17.310
then you might not have captured it.

00:28:17.310 --> 00:28:22.310
But you did and then
there was that response

00:28:22.670 --> 00:28:24.560
and the response was just like,

00:28:24.560 --> 00:28:26.240
oh my God, A I'm not alone.

00:28:26.240 --> 00:28:28.890
B, I like this feeling probably.

00:28:28.890 --> 00:28:30.370
- Right.
- And maybe it sounds like

00:28:30.370 --> 00:28:31.830
that's one of the things
that clued you off to

00:28:31.830 --> 00:28:32.890
like I can be a home base,

00:28:32.890 --> 00:28:34.120
maybe I can be a home base.

00:28:34.120 --> 00:28:36.800
- Well I was very aware
that the vulnerability

00:28:36.800 --> 00:28:39.150
was the thing that people
were connecting with.

00:28:39.150 --> 00:28:41.780
And when I got the
opportunity to write a book

00:28:41.780 --> 00:28:46.780
I understood that that had to be the key

00:28:47.380 --> 00:28:51.530
sort of through line throughout
the entire narrative.

00:28:51.530 --> 00:28:53.793
Because let's face it I'm not,

00:28:54.840 --> 00:28:56.970
it's not like I won
some World Championship.

00:28:56.970 --> 00:28:59.640
I've never won a race,
I've done some crazy things

00:28:59.640 --> 00:29:01.240
in ultra-endurance but there's plenty

00:29:01.240 --> 00:29:03.700
of athletes out there
they're a lot better than me,

00:29:03.700 --> 00:29:05.010
that are more talented than me,

00:29:05.010 --> 00:29:07.370
then are more accomplished than me.

00:29:07.370 --> 00:29:12.370
So why am I being given an
opportunity to write a book?

00:29:12.610 --> 00:29:14.010
Like it's weird, right?

00:29:14.010 --> 00:29:16.900
It doesn't, on paper it didn't
really seem to make sense.

00:29:16.900 --> 00:29:21.060
And so I was very aware
that the only reason

00:29:21.060 --> 00:29:25.780
that people would connect with my story

00:29:25.780 --> 00:29:27.870
was going to be directly
related to the extent

00:29:27.870 --> 00:29:30.700
to which I was willing to be vulnerable

00:29:30.700 --> 00:29:34.010
and talk about things
that aren't so comfortable

00:29:34.010 --> 00:29:36.600
and that I'm not that proud of.

00:29:36.600 --> 00:29:38.720
So the process of writing it really

00:29:38.720 --> 00:29:41.040
was one of just getting into the mindset

00:29:41.040 --> 00:29:43.835
of private journaling.

00:29:43.835 --> 00:29:47.630
I had to make it like a diary
that no one was gonna read.

00:29:47.630 --> 00:29:50.190
And then I would have
these moments where--

00:29:50.190 --> 00:29:51.610
I can't believe--
- Oh my God wait,

00:29:51.610 --> 00:29:52.740
this is gonna be a book?

00:29:52.740 --> 00:29:56.143
I would freak out and be
paralyzed for several days.

00:29:57.080 --> 00:29:58.940
But in retrospect looking back,

00:29:58.940 --> 00:30:01.170
I know that that's why the
book has been successful

00:30:01.170 --> 00:30:02.850
because it's the humanity.

00:30:02.850 --> 00:30:04.540
Because everybody can find some aspect

00:30:04.540 --> 00:30:09.540
of their own journey in my
pain points or my struggles.

00:30:10.430 --> 00:30:13.460
My story isn't that remarkable,

00:30:13.460 --> 00:30:14.980
the things that I've gone through.

00:30:14.980 --> 00:30:17.260
Many people have gone through far worse

00:30:17.260 --> 00:30:21.000
than what I've had to
endure to get to this place.

00:30:21.000 --> 00:30:24.470
But I think there's there's
an integrity in that honesty,

00:30:24.470 --> 00:30:26.030
and I think people respond to that.

00:30:26.030 --> 00:30:27.850
They know when it's real.

00:30:27.850 --> 00:30:30.030
- Do you think that that true north

00:30:30.030 --> 00:30:32.140
or that beacon that thing that's inside of

00:30:33.470 --> 00:30:34.613
in this case we're talking about you,

00:30:34.613 --> 00:30:37.593
that was inside of you, is
that inside of everybody?

00:30:38.430 --> 00:30:40.210
Or is that something you have to find,

00:30:40.210 --> 00:30:43.480
is it natively there do
you have to create it?

00:30:43.480 --> 00:30:46.313
How do people understand their true north?

00:30:48.050 --> 00:30:49.280
- I don't know that

00:30:52.090 --> 00:30:54.010
there's only one true north.

00:30:54.010 --> 00:30:57.950
Maybe there's many for people
but I think the process

00:30:57.950 --> 00:31:02.940
of trying to unlock that or
discover that within oneself

00:31:03.900 --> 00:31:07.200
is a journey of
self-discovery that requires

00:31:07.200 --> 00:31:10.460
rigorous self-honesty and rigorous

00:31:12.300 --> 00:31:15.660
adherence to one's personal truth.

00:31:15.660 --> 00:31:18.180
And I think a lot of
people are walking around

00:31:18.180 --> 00:31:20.470
not understanding what
that is for themselves.

00:31:20.470 --> 00:31:21.850
Like what do you mean my personal truth

00:31:21.850 --> 00:31:24.430
like I'm just going to work
man, I'm trying to like--

00:31:24.430 --> 00:31:26.123
- Make buck bro.
- Yeah exactly.

00:31:27.360 --> 00:31:30.390
So in order to really connect with that

00:31:30.390 --> 00:31:32.033
I think it's an inside job.

00:31:33.630 --> 00:31:35.864
You can go out and ride your bike all day

00:31:35.864 --> 00:31:40.300
or do jiu-jitsu or lose a bunch of weight,

00:31:40.300 --> 00:31:43.660
but ultimately it's about
your relationship with you.

00:31:43.660 --> 00:31:46.020
And that will be revealed to you

00:31:46.020 --> 00:31:50.550
only in the moments in which you are

00:31:50.550 --> 00:31:52.550
allowing yourself to get quiet enough.

00:31:52.550 --> 00:31:54.350
Where you can shut off the thinking brain

00:31:54.350 --> 00:31:57.250
or you can become an
observer of your own thoughts

00:31:57.250 --> 00:31:59.970
and connect with your own consciousness.

00:31:59.970 --> 00:32:03.210
And in that relationship as it develops

00:32:03.210 --> 00:32:05.890
through meditation or mindfulness practice

00:32:05.890 --> 00:32:09.653
or whatever strategy you employ.

00:32:10.827 --> 00:32:13.520
I think that your higher
conscious will tell you

00:32:14.500 --> 00:32:16.420
who it is and what it wants to be.

00:32:16.420 --> 00:32:21.420
And your job then becomes
piecing that together,

00:32:21.710 --> 00:32:24.413
slowly over a very long period of time.

00:32:25.320 --> 00:32:26.635
- For you is that--

00:32:26.635 --> 00:32:28.120
- Does that sound too obtuse?

00:32:28.120 --> 00:32:29.710
- Not only is that not obtuse,

00:32:29.710 --> 00:32:32.000
it's poetic, it was beautiful.

00:32:32.000 --> 00:32:34.090
Kind of just like letting it land there.

00:32:34.090 --> 00:32:37.430
So for you was that the trail,

00:32:37.430 --> 00:32:40.440
was that moment of quiet,
the time the reflection,

00:32:40.440 --> 00:32:45.440
was that the trail and
the ocean and the path?

00:32:46.150 --> 00:32:49.210
- It was all of those things
and it was meditation,

00:32:49.210 --> 00:32:51.560
and it was connecting with my body

00:32:51.560 --> 00:32:53.310
for the first time in a really long time.

00:32:53.310 --> 00:32:56.520
Again it was about learning how to connect

00:32:56.520 --> 00:32:58.680
with my instincts and then trust them.

00:32:58.680 --> 00:32:59.580
- Yeah.

00:32:59.580 --> 00:33:01.180
- And these are all things

00:33:01.180 --> 00:33:03.830
that I originally started to learn about

00:33:03.830 --> 00:33:07.000
as a result of getting
sober and being in 12-step

00:33:07.000 --> 00:33:09.700
and understanding that
we're spiritual beings

00:33:09.700 --> 00:33:10.970
having a human experience.

00:33:10.970 --> 00:33:13.670
Like these were all crazy
foreign concepts to me.

00:33:13.670 --> 00:33:16.840
I had a decade spent in church basements

00:33:16.840 --> 00:33:20.300
and with fellow alcoholics
and drug addicts

00:33:20.300 --> 00:33:23.920
to acquaint me with some of these concepts

00:33:23.920 --> 00:33:27.570
that I then started to delve deeper into.

00:33:27.570 --> 00:33:31.650
And the physical aspect of these things

00:33:31.650 --> 00:33:35.670
that I've done are just one
avenue of exploration for that,

00:33:35.670 --> 00:33:36.830
but I think there's many

00:33:36.830 --> 00:33:39.120
and it's different for everybody.

00:33:39.120 --> 00:33:40.070
- You talked about meditation,

00:33:40.070 --> 00:33:42.840
mindfulness, exercise, a church basement,

00:33:42.840 --> 00:33:43.770
any others come to mind?

00:33:43.770 --> 00:33:45.520
- It can be your faith-based community,

00:33:45.520 --> 00:33:47.790
it can be your relationship
with your kids.

00:33:47.790 --> 00:33:49.080
It can be sitting in a cave,

00:33:49.080 --> 00:33:50.740
it can be of a personal retreat.

00:33:50.740 --> 00:33:54.510
It can be like I just
said, learning jiu-jitsu,

00:33:54.510 --> 00:33:56.770
it can be going out in nature

00:33:56.770 --> 00:33:59.350
and taking photographs,
it could be what you do.

00:33:59.350 --> 00:34:03.710
I think it's about finding
what lights your own spark

00:34:03.710 --> 00:34:06.240
and then trusting your instincts enough

00:34:06.240 --> 00:34:09.542
to pull on that thread
and continue to follow it

00:34:09.542 --> 00:34:11.760
with the understanding that more

00:34:11.760 --> 00:34:14.810
will be revealed to you in time.

00:34:14.810 --> 00:34:17.740
- So was it a Rumi quote I don't remember

00:34:17.740 --> 00:34:20.830
we're gonna botch this
but it's a fair to say

00:34:20.830 --> 00:34:24.190
I'm gonna try and summarize
but someone else's quote.

00:34:24.190 --> 00:34:26.680
That you don't have to
see the whole staircase

00:34:26.680 --> 00:34:28.710
you just have to find the first stair.

00:34:28.710 --> 00:34:29.980
- I think that's super profound.

00:34:29.980 --> 00:34:34.030
I think so many people especially

00:34:34.030 --> 00:34:37.830
in this kind of self-help
rubric or universe

00:34:37.830 --> 00:34:40.160
that we're kind of part of,

00:34:40.160 --> 00:34:43.700
everybody wants to know all
the steps before they begin.

00:34:43.700 --> 00:34:44.710
- Because then they're gonna decide,

00:34:44.710 --> 00:34:45.700
they're gonna say hmm.

00:34:45.700 --> 00:34:46.533
- [Rich] Yeah.

00:34:46.533 --> 00:34:49.390
- First to get hard and
I have to sweat and cry.

00:34:49.390 --> 00:34:50.480
- Right.
- And bleed for this,

00:34:50.480 --> 00:34:52.450
I'm not sure I want it so can you show me

00:34:52.450 --> 00:34:53.980
what it looks like around the corner.

00:34:53.980 --> 00:34:56.070
And most people that I
know that are already good

00:34:56.070 --> 00:34:58.661
they're like sorry there that's just,

00:34:58.661 --> 00:35:00.060
you've got to take the first...

00:35:00.060 --> 00:35:01.340
- You gotta take the first step.

00:35:01.340 --> 00:35:05.060
I mean use running as
an example like well,

00:35:05.060 --> 00:35:06.050
what watch do I need?

00:35:06.050 --> 00:35:07.160
What shoes do I need?

00:35:07.160 --> 00:35:09.660
I need my training plan, is
that the right training plan

00:35:09.660 --> 00:35:10.830
or should I do this training plan?

00:35:10.830 --> 00:35:12.600
Which race should I sign up for?

00:35:12.600 --> 00:35:15.880
Its analysis paralysis that
keeps people stuck forever

00:35:15.880 --> 00:35:20.710
because they wanna
understand the entire journey

00:35:20.710 --> 00:35:21.920
from beginning to end.

00:35:21.920 --> 00:35:22.753
- [Chase] Yeah.

00:35:22.753 --> 00:35:24.370
- And what they're failing
to realize or understand

00:35:24.370 --> 00:35:28.960
or embrace is that the beauty
of the whole experience

00:35:28.960 --> 00:35:31.860
is in the unknowing, that's
where the faith comes in.

00:35:31.860 --> 00:35:35.040
You take that first step and it's just fog

00:35:35.040 --> 00:35:38.593
in front of you, you don't
know and you have to trust.

00:35:39.560 --> 00:35:42.580
And you have to be willing
to take that leap of faith

00:35:42.580 --> 00:35:46.850
into the unknown and believe
that you will be caught,

00:35:46.850 --> 00:35:51.030
that you will be cradled
somehow and that's scary.

00:35:51.030 --> 00:35:52.250
- Yeah
- It's frightening.

00:35:52.250 --> 00:35:53.500
It was frightening for me

00:35:55.260 --> 00:35:58.853
but that's the magic man.

00:35:59.740 --> 00:36:03.880
And I don't wanna deprive
somebody of that experience

00:36:03.880 --> 00:36:05.880
because that's where all the beauty

00:36:05.880 --> 00:36:10.070
and the self understanding and the faith

00:36:10.070 --> 00:36:13.453
and the sense of self comes from.

00:36:15.210 --> 00:36:16.483
- You have four kids.

00:36:17.910 --> 00:36:22.380
How are you, how or what are you doing

00:36:22.380 --> 00:36:26.380
to imprint some of this
just gold into their lives?

00:36:26.380 --> 00:36:28.560
Is there parenthood,
(Rich coughs)

00:36:28.560 --> 00:36:29.840
now this is parenting advice

00:36:29.840 --> 00:36:33.490
or it's just a comment or sort of trying

00:36:33.490 --> 00:36:36.643
to understand humanity, but are you?

00:36:37.630 --> 00:36:38.463
- Well.

00:36:39.360 --> 00:36:41.770
- The chance of them
listening to this are low.

00:36:41.770 --> 00:36:43.327
- Trust me they're not gonna listen.

00:36:43.327 --> 00:36:44.160
(Rich laughs)
- Yeah, exactly.

00:36:44.160 --> 00:36:45.510
- They couldn't be less interested

00:36:45.510 --> 00:36:49.243
in anything that I'm doing, but--

00:36:49.243 --> 00:36:50.660
- What are their ages?

00:36:50.660 --> 00:36:51.738
- So--

00:36:51.738 --> 00:36:52.571
- Unless if you're...

00:36:52.571 --> 00:36:57.130
- So I've got two boys,
they are my stepsons

00:36:57.130 --> 00:36:58.740
that I've lived with since
they were three and four

00:36:58.740 --> 00:37:00.960
but they're now 22 and 23.

00:37:00.960 --> 00:37:02.870
And they've moved out of the house,

00:37:02.870 --> 00:37:07.690
they're musicians and a band
with my nephew, their cousin.

00:37:07.690 --> 00:37:09.590
And they're working on their first album,

00:37:09.590 --> 00:37:11.260
so they're pursuing their dream

00:37:11.260 --> 00:37:12.457
and they're incredibly talented.

00:37:12.457 --> 00:37:14.810
I have no doubt that they'll be successful

00:37:14.810 --> 00:37:17.230
they're kind of embedded
into the music scene

00:37:17.230 --> 00:37:20.150
of East Los Angeles and it's super cool

00:37:20.150 --> 00:37:22.080
to see them fully engaged

00:37:22.080 --> 00:37:23.780
in what they wanna be
doing with their lives.

00:37:23.780 --> 00:37:27.163
Then I've got two daughters
that are 15 and 11.

00:37:28.610 --> 00:37:31.520
15 year old daughter it's a tricky,

00:37:31.520 --> 00:37:33.200
that's a tricky universe.

00:37:33.200 --> 00:37:36.000
And she's a visual artist and she goes

00:37:36.000 --> 00:37:40.010
to an Arts High School
in downtown Los Angeles.

00:37:40.010 --> 00:37:43.100
That's required our family
to kind of reconfigure

00:37:43.100 --> 00:37:45.760
how we live because it's very
far from our other house.

00:37:45.760 --> 00:37:49.033
So my wife and I are now splitting time,

00:37:49.033 --> 00:37:51.910
staying in an apartment that we rented

